module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorAlgebraDeterminant

/-!
# The determinant of a sheaf of modules generated by local sections

Let `O` be a sheaf of commutative rings on a site, let `F` be a sheaf of `O`-modules with a
bundle of tensor, exterior and symmetric algebras `A`, and let `det(F) ⊆ ⋀(F)` be the
annihilator of the degree-one part
(`SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.exteriorAnnihilator`). By definition a local
section of `⋀ⁿ F` over `U` lies in `det(F)` when its restriction along **every** arrow out of
`U` is killed by **every** degree-one section there — the quantification over arrows is what
makes the family of annihilators a subpresheaf at all, since the sectionwise annihilators are
not stable under restriction.

This file identifies that condition with a finite, sectionwise one as soon as `F` is generated
below `U` by a family of sections over `U`: the restriction of the section along every arrow is
killed by every degree-one section there exactly when the section itself is killed by the
members of the generating family.

This is the point the Stacks Project marks as having details omitted in the proof of Tag 0FJN:
*"one has to be careful as annihilators cannot be defined as the sheafification of taking
annihilators on sections over opens"*. On a trivialising open the sheaf of a flat module of
finite presentation is a direct summand of `O_U^{⊕n}` (Tag 08BL,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyFiniteFreeSummand_of_isFlat_of_isFinitePresentation`), hence
generated below `U` by the `n` images of the basis sections, and that is exactly the hypothesis
below.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.GeneratesBelow`: a family of sections of `F` over `U` generates `F` below `U`
  when every section of `F` over every `V` with an arrow `U ⟶ V` is a finite `O(V)`-combination
  of the restrictions of the family.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.isExteriorAnnihilated_iff_of_generatesBelow`:
  **for `F` generated below `U` by `s`, a local section of `⋀ⁿ F` over `U` is exterior
  annihilated exactly when it is killed by the degree-one sections attached to the `s i`.**
* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.mem_exteriorAnnihilator_iff_of_generatesBelow`:
  the same statement as a membership criterion for `exteriorAnnihilator`.

## Implementation notes

`GeneratesBelow` is phrased with an explicit finite combination rather than as
`Submodule.span _ _ = ⊤`, so that the induction in the proof is `Finset.induction` on the
index set of the combination and no submodule has to be produced and shown to be the top one.
The two formulations are interchangeable by `Submodule.mem_span_finset`.

The nontrivial direction unwinds the two naturalities of Section 17.21's package: the
degree-one generator `A.exteriorGenerator` is a morphism of sheaves of modules, so it commutes
with restriction, and the multiplication `A.exterior.mul 1 n` is a `Stacks.BilinearMap`, so it
is `O`-bilinear and commutes with restriction. A generator of the combination therefore
contributes the restriction of a product already known to vanish over `U`, and the coefficients
come out of the product by linearity in the first variable.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FJN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08BL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08BL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CH)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe v u w

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  {Osharp : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- A family `s` of local sections of `F` over `U` **generates `F` below `U`** when every local
section of `F` over an object `V` equipped with an arrow `U ⟶ V` is a finite `O(V)`-linear
combination of the restrictions of the `s i` along that arrow.

On the site of opens of a space, with `U` an open and `V ⊆ U`, this says that the restrictions
of the `s i` to `V` generate `F(V)` as an `O(V)`-module — which is what a retraction of `F|_U`
off `O_U^{⊕n}` provides, with `s` the images of the basis sections. -/
def GeneratesBelow (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp))
    {U : Cᵒᵖ} {ι : Type*} (s : ι → F.val.obj U) : Prop :=
  ∀ (V : Cᵒᵖ) (f : U ⟶ V) (m : F.val.obj V),
    ∃ (t : Finset ι) (c : ι → (CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp).obj.obj V),
      m = ∑ i ∈ t, c i • F.val.restrictₛₗ f (s i)

namespace TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras

variable {F : SheafOfModules.{w} (CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp)}
  (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras J F) (n : ℕ)

/-- **A local section of `⋀ⁿ F` over `U` is exterior annihilated as soon as it is killed by the
degree-one sections of a family generating `F` below `U`.**

This is the direction that does the work: the condition defining `det(F)` quantifies over all
arrows out of `U` and all degree-one sections there, and the hypothesis only constrains finitely
many sections over `U` itself. -/
theorem isExteriorAnnihilated_of_generatesBelow {U : Cᵒᵖ} {ι : Type*} {s : ι → F.val.obj U}
    (hs : GeneratesBelow F s) (x : (A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)
    (hx : ∀ i, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).app U
      (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) x = 0) :
    A.IsExteriorAnnihilated n x := by
  classical
  intro V f m
  -- Each restricted generator contributes a restriction of a product that already vanishes.
  have hgen : ∀ i, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).app V
      (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app V (F.val.restrictₛₗ f (s i)))
      ((A.exteriorPower n).val.restrictₛₗ f x) = 0 := by
    intro i
    rw [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply, PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply,
      PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply A.exteriorGenerator.val f (s i),
      ← (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).naturality f (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) x, hx i]
    exact map_zero _
  obtain ⟨t, c, rfl⟩ := hs V f m
  induction t using Finset.induction with
  | empty => rw [Finset.sum_empty, map_zero, map_zero, AddMonoidHom.zero_apply]
  | insert i t hi ih =>
      rw [Finset.sum_insert hi, map_add, map_add, AddMonoidHom.add_apply, ih, add_zero,
        map_smul, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).map_smul_left, hgen i, smul_zero]

/-- **For `F` generated below `U` by `s`, exterior annihilation over `U` is annihilation by the
degree-one sections attached to the `s i`.** -/
theorem isExteriorAnnihilated_iff_of_generatesBelow {U : Cᵒᵖ} {ι : Type*}
    {s : ι → F.val.obj U} (hs : GeneratesBelow F s) (x : (A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U) :
    A.IsExteriorAnnihilated n x ↔
      ∀ i, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).app U
        (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) x = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun hx i => ?_, A.isExteriorAnnihilated_of_generatesBelow n hs x⟩
  have h := hx U (𝟙 U) (s i)
  rwa [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply, PresheafOfModules.map_id_apply] at h

/-- `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.isExteriorAnnihilated_iff_of_generatesBelow`
as a membership criterion for the degree-`n` summand of `det(F)`. -/
theorem mem_exteriorAnnihilator_iff_of_generatesBelow {U : Cᵒᵖ} {ι : Type*}
    {s : ι → F.val.obj U} (hs : GeneratesBelow F s) (x : (A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U) :
    x ∈ (A.exteriorAnnihilator n).toSubmodule.obj U ↔
      ∀ i, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).app U
        (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (s i)) x = 0 :=
  A.isExteriorAnnihilated_iff_of_generatesBelow n hs x

end TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras

end SheafOfModules

end
